<section class="hero">
  {% include "partials/ambient-log.njk" %}
  <div class="wrap" style="position: relative; z-index: 1;">
    <h1>Twenty years on<br>one question.</h1>
    <p class="hero__lead">
      How do you deploy a system that decides things on a person's behalf, somewhere being wrong is
      expensive, and get people to trust it enough to actually use it? I've worked on it in eight
      settings, from a special operations exoskeleton to a 911 call center to an institutional AI
      platform. PhD in Systems Engineering.
    </p>
    <div class="hero__ctas">
      <a href="/work/" class="btn btn-primary">View Full Work &rarr;</a>
      <a href="/contact/" class="btn btn-ghost-dark">Get in Touch</a>
    </div>
    <div class="hero__credentials">
      <div class="hero__credential">
        <div class="value">PhD</div>
        <div class="label">Systems Engineering</div>
      </div>
      <div class="hero__credential">
        <div class="value">$45M</div>
        <div class="label">Portfolio, 14 Programs</div>
      </div>
      <div class="hero__credential">
        <div class="value">75x</div>
        <div class="label">SaaS Adoption, IBM</div>
      </div>
      <div class="hero__credential">
        <div class="value">64%</div>
        <div class="label">Sales Growth, Blackboard</div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section wrap">
  <div class="split-cta">
    <div class="split-cta__panel is-primary">
      <div class="eyebrow" style="color: rgba(247,244,239,0.55);">Evaluating me for a role</div>
      <h2>I want a bigger platform to run AI on. Not a bigger title.</h2>
      <p>Senior, Lead or Principal product and strategy roles, somewhere with the scale to build AI systems that hold up. Track record's below.</p>
      <a href="/work/" class="btn btn-ghost-dark">View Full Work &rarr;</a>
    </div>
    <div class="split-cta__panel">
      <div class="eyebrow">Need AI built or governed</div>
      <h2>Redfearn Group takes the engagement your team is stuck on.</h2>
      <p>AI strategy. LLM agent architecture. Governance frameworks that satisfy legal without slowing engineering down.</p>
      <a href="mailto:{{ site.email }}" class="btn btn-ghost">Email {{ site.email }} &rarr;</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section section--border-top" id="through-line">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="section-label">The Through-Line</div>
    <h2>One question, eight settings.</h2>
    <p class="lead" style="max-width: 640px;">The domain changed each time. The question did not.</p>
    <div class="card-grid card-grid--quad" style="margin-top: 2.5rem;">
      <a href="/publications/ux-engineering-adoption-practice/" class="card">
        <div class="eyebrow">01 &middot; 2010 to 2013</div>
        <h3>MS thesis, BYU</h3>
        <p class="small">What an organization pays when it adopts an unfamiliar practice. The enterprise AI adoption problem, before the AI.</p>
      </a>
      <a href="/publications/rapid-design-prototyping-mixed-reality/" class="card">
        <div class="eyebrow">02 &middot; 2012 to 2017</div>
        <h3>PhD dissertation, Virginia Tech</h3>
        <p class="small">What an intelligent system should surface to an operator under load, when it should defer to the human, and how it should fail safely.</p>
      </a>
      <a href="/work/talos-human-ai-interaction/" class="card">
        <div class="eyebrow">03 &middot; 2014 to 2017</div>
        <h3>TALOS, Special Operations Command</h3>
        <p class="small">The human-AI interaction model for a powered exoskeleton, worked out on site with operators under hard safety constraints.</p>
      </a>
      <a href="/work/byu-innovation-lab/" class="card">
        <div class="eyebrow">04 &middot; 2018 to 2020</div>
        <h3>Advanced HCI, BYU</h3>
        <p class="small">A curriculum built around adaptive interfaces: how people direct, correct, and override systems that decide for them.</p>
      </a>
      <a href="/work/portfolio-leadership/" class="card">
        <div class="eyebrow">05 &middot; 2018 to 2024</div>
        <h3>Army Cyber Institute, West Point</h3>
        <p class="small">Applied LLM research on adversarial AI risk in critical infrastructure, and two published assessments.</p>
      </a>
      <a href="/work/emergency-services-modernization/" class="card">
        <div class="eyebrow">06 &middot; 2024 to 2026</div>
        <h3>Next Generation 9&#8209;1&#8209;1</h3>
        <p class="small">Whether AI can be trusted inside a 911 call center, where a wrong output costs a life.</p>
      </a>
      <a href="/work/ai-platform-architecture/" class="card">
        <div class="eyebrow">07 &middot; 2026</div>
        <h3>Institutional AI platform</h3>
        <p class="small">The product spec for an enterprise AI platform serving more than 200,000 learners.</p>
      </a>
      <a href="/title-15-amendment-analysis/" class="card">
        <div class="eyebrow">08 &middot; 2026</div>
        <h3>Title 15 analysis, Spanish Fork</h3>
        <p class="small">Publishing the weights: an independent public analysis with every calculation shown, so anyone can check whether the conclusion survives.</p>
      </a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

